        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0164" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/558.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mutineers in possession of Wuchang. The Taotai requested the foreign gunboat to
                    patrol river to prevent mutineers crossing, but the consuls agreed to ignore the
                    request. Defense will be made only of the concessions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
